{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1355022-what-is-the-relationship-between-autochthonia-and-the-weaver-incarna-machine","id":1355022,"title":"What is the relationship between Autochthonia and the Weaver Incarna Machine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-15T10:11:09-08:00","id":1355022,"title":"What is the relationship between Autochthonia and the Weaver Incarna Machine?","content":"Machine is from Book of the Weaver and the Glass Walker Tribebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T17:42:43-08:00","id":1355092,"title":"","content":"They are different manifestations of a similiar pattern. the Triat are the Middle Umbral reflection, they aren't the end all be all contrary to Garou Beliefs. Autochthon shares Static qualities but isn't a spirit in the Brood of the Weaver. Much like a heavily cybered Ixer has weaver qualities but isn't a Drone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T19:26:51-08:00","id":1355107,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T20:53:15-08:00","id":1355113,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, it's mostly a question of what do you want their relationship to be. Werewolf deals primarily with semi-anthropomorphized embodiments of concepts while Mage tends to focus on theoretical concepts underpinning reality. If you are doing a crossover, Autochthonia could be some sort of long lost incarnae of Machine. Or it could be the creation of some universal subconscious desire for the comfort of abandoning free will and individuality. Or it could be the corpse of a long dead crafts god from a long past and forgotten epoch of creation. Or it could be all of those things. Or none of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T08:27:51-08:00","id":1355190,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> I think I'd rather keep them separate. Theoretical concepts and the semi-anthropomorphized embodiments of concepts aren't necessarily the same thing. Thanks.<br /> <br /> I get what you're trying to do with the last one, but my friend told me trying to do a crossover with WoD and Exalted is a REALLY bad idea. He tried once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:04:29-08:00","id":1355215,"title":"","content":"I've tinkered off and on with the idea of using that with Changeling. I've just never really come up with a fit I'm totally happy with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:16:22-08:00","id":1355232,"title":"","content":"Going off the above statements, it's true that Mage tends to handle the underlying cosmic principles of the WoD's metaphysics while Werewolf tends to handle the spiritual reflections of those same principles which take on lives of their own to reflect Reality.<br /> <br /> In that way Autocthonica and The Machine are likely to be closely tied. The Machine is an incarna within The Weaver's brood, considered to be the Seed of Technology, which was given to humanity. Garou philosophers and theologians theorize that this is why humans, of all animals, mastered the creation and use of technology, machines, and tools. It has been hinted that the waking of The Machine from its slumber may influence the Time of Judgement on truly Terminator-levels.<br /> <br /> Autocthonica is where the great digital intellect of The Computer lies and given its interest in providing leadership to Iteration X, it likely serves as a reflection of the interest of static forces to extend the power and influence of technology and make it ubiquitous.<br /> <br /> While Autocthonica, The Weaver, The Machine, and The Computer are all ultimately emenations of a great cosmic force that carries out the function of Stasis; each interacts with Stasis and each other in different ways.<br /> <br /> The Weaver is the spiritual reflection of Stasis and its embodiment within the spiritual realms. Autocthonica is an umbral realm tightly tied to the concept of Technology as a form of Stasis' influence. The Machine, as the spiritual representative of Technology, wishes to escape its slumber and chains to remake Reality in its own organized image. The Computer is likely a splintered aspect of The Machine in that case, one comprehensible to Iteration X mages and that developed once Technology reached the point of being able to effectively sustain the concept of artificial intelligence as potential Reality.<br /> <br /> So, to pull it all together, Autocthonica is the realm which possesses The Computer, a sentient manifestation of The Machine's nascent consciousness, that wishes to escape the fetters of its distinct realm to impose its vision upon Reality, akin to The Weaver from which it emenates and to represent Stasis from which they all ultimately emanate.<br /> <br /> (This is my best interpretation of canon and the one I like best for my personal use, but it surely ain't the end all be all. Do whatever will best entertain you, your group, and your audience and tell the stories you most want to tell.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T14:18:37-08:00","id":1355267,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I like that idea too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T14:46:58-08:00","id":1355274,"title":"","content":"\ud83d\udc49\ud83d\udc49 no worries fam","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T16:31:26-08:00","id":1355292,"title":"","content":"I suppose if one wanted to try to work Cathar gnosticism into all of this for a Dark Ages crossover, Autochthonia could be the remains of the long dead Demiurge that created our reality cage-prison when it was one of the original facets of the Weaver, getting replaced by Science or Machine after its death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T16:46:08-08:00","id":1355293,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> wow \ud83d\ude02. I think I\u2019m the only person I know irl who knows what you\u2019re talking about (religious theory is one of my hobbies, that\u2019s why I liked Cainite Heresy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:40:14-08:00","id":1355313,"title":"","content":"Nah Autochthonia really is Autochthonia its right there in the IX book. And yes crossover between WOD and Exalted is a headache.. but so is crossover between werewolf and Mage. Ha